{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a goat.</b> Rashi's explanation: when you arrive at the bulls and rams, they are not the same, etc. That is, here it is written ופר בן בקר אחד ואלים שנים, and when you arrive at the section of Pinchas you find written פרים בני בקר שנים ואיל אחד. And furthermore, if you wish to say, these are the additional offerings of the section of Pinchas — what distinguishes the additional offerings of Atzeret, that they are written here, and what distinguishes the additional offerings of the other festivals, that they are not written except in the section of Pinchas?" "<b>And two lambs of the first year.</b> R. Shimon said: for what do the two lambs of Atzeret atone? For contamination of the Temple and its holy things. And if the first atoned, for what does the second come? Is it not for contamination that occurred between this one and that one? Say henceforth: thus Israel would need [an offering] at every moment, but HaKadosh Baruch Hu had compassion on Israel."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:35.883139645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}